<!--
  Vendored cryptobyte's binary breaks at 1.26.10.3, read by the release's binary-compatibility guard
  (src/tools/pushnuget/GoApiCompat.psm1; docs/phase4/DESIGN-binary-compat-guard.md).

  Every entry is batch 235 (C2, claude/c2-thisref-box): a pointer method that calls a value method on its own
  receiver is emitted over the box, so these five exported pointer methods take this ж<String> where 1.26.10.2
  took this ref String.

  NOT REACHABLE BY A CONSUMER, so no release-notes line (whole-surface census, 2026-11-07):
  - Go's std-vendored packages are importable only by the standard library. A module that imports
    golang.org/x/crypto/cryptobyte gets the real x/crypto module, never this package.
  - Its one caller is crypto/x509 (parser.cs). go.crypto.x509 pins this package EXACTLY ([1.26.10.2] at .2,
    [build] at .3), so a .2 x509 with a .3 cryptobyte is refused at restore and never bound at run time.

  Baseline: the published go.vendor.golang.org.x.crypto.cryptobyte 1.26.10.2. When 1.26.10.3 is published it
  becomes the baseline, every entry here matches nothing, and the guard reads each one RED as unnecessary: delete
  this file then.
-->
